Prevent premature interruption of Bastion tower RPG and rubble search sequence

Allow the Bastion tower launch and subsequent rubble search to continue across a wider camera range.

Implementation
planTower() reduces the planned firing stance clamp from origin/view +236/+228 to +224/+224, while retaining a minimum of BASTION_TOWER.x +76.

towerFramed() and searchFramed() change margin from -48 to -160 while their corresponding sequence is active, and from -20 to -120 while preparing it. These negative margins deliberately admit actors outside the nominal viewport.

Fourth-district aftermath activation clamps the initial actor x to yard.origin +216 and widens activation checks. Other districts retain their story x.

HypotheticalDevastation.nextScenicTick() permits the fourth-district player position up to center +230 during the authored contact interval, instead of center +108; the other districts keep +108.

Timing and limitations
Only HypotheticalAftermath.ts and HypotheticalDevastation.ts change. There are no new art files, audio cues, tests or authoring captures.

The patch changes scene eligibility and clock suspension, not projectile damage or tower physics. It retains the 36-step abort counter already added in 4057d1a. Its purpose is to avoid premature interruption; no new gameplay observation is inferred from the source patch.

